You can set the execution context selector in Chrome DevTools through the console using several methods. Here are the most effective approaches:

## Method 1: Using `debugger` Statement with Context

```javascript
// This will pause execution in the current context
debugger;

// After pausing, you can use the console in that context
```

## Method 2: Using `console.assert` with Context

```javascript
// Set a breakpoint conditionally
console.assert(false, 'Pause here');
```

## Method 3: Programmatic Context Switching

```javascript
// Switch to a specific frame/context
// In the console, you can use:
window.frames[0].console.log('In iframe context');

// Or for specific elements
document.querySelector('iframe').contentWindow.console.log('In iframe');
```

## Method 4: Using `debug` Command

```javascript
// In the console, type:
debug(functionName);
// This will automatically pause when that function is called
```

